description: Agora bounded context — scope required before any work
alwaysApply: true
---

No active Agora Context is selected.

Do not search, read, edit, or run commands until scope is set.

Repo-wide counting, searching, grepping, listing, and shell commands also require scope first.

Ask the user once:

> **Scope required:**
> **A — Focus** (Agora Context → ✓ → Confirm → **New Agent chat**)
> **B — Skip** (full repo)
>
> Reply with A or B to proceed.

If the user chooses **A**: explain how to set focus in Agora Context, then stop.

After focus is confirmed, the user must start a **New Agent chat**. Do not reuse an old chat tab — Cursor keeps prior chat context.

If the user chooses **B**: proceed with full repo access.

If the user names explicit file paths in their message, use only those paths and do not ask for scope.
